proxy design pattern is one of the structural design pattern
proxy means substitute or placeholder
It provides a Surrogate Object to control access to the original object.

Real-Time Example
Think about 🔥 YouTube Video Streaming:

When you click on a video thumbnail, it shows the Preview Image (Proxy Object) first.
Only if you click the play button, the Actual Video will start loading (Real Object).

why proxy design pattern ?
1.> To Control Access to the real object
2.> To improve performance by delaying heavy object creation.
3.> To provide security
4.> caching mechanism.

Types of Proxy Design Pattern
Type                   	Purpose	                           Real-Time Example
Virtual Proxy	        Lazy Initialization	               Hibernate Lazy Loading
Protection Proxy	    Access Control	                   Spring Security
Cache Proxy         	Caching Heavy Objects              Redis Cache
Remote Proxy         	Communication with Remote Object   Microservices Feign Client
Smart Proxy	            Adding Extra Functionality	       AOP Logging


Spring Framework Uses Proxy Design Pattern Internally
Class Name               	Proxy Type	                         Purpose
Hibernate	                Virtual Proxy	                     Lazy Initialization
Spring Security	            Protection Proxy	                 Access Control
Feign Client	            Remote Proxy	                     Microservices Call
Spring AOP	                Smart Proxy	                         Logging & Transactions
Redis Cache	                Cache Proxy	                         Caching

 Proxy Design Pattern is one of the Most Common Design Patterns used in
✅ Hibernate
✅ Spring Security
✅ Feign Client
✅ Spring AOP